  "question": {
    "text": "If the time period $t$ of the oscillation of a drop of liquid of density $d$, radius $r$, vibrating under surface tension $s$ is given by the formula $t=\\sqrt{r^{2 b} s^c d^{a / 2}}$. It is observed that the time period is directly proportional to $\\sqrt{\\frac{d}{s}}$. The value of $b$ should therefore be :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
